course: dictionary
lesson: 841
title: Berlin, a name for a place
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Berlin is a name, and a name starts with a capital letter. Berlin is the capital city of Germany and its largest city. A capital is where a country's government works, so Berlin is the place that runs the country.
explain: Berlin has a famous history. During the Cold War the city was divided into East Berlin and West Berlin by the Berlin Wall. When the Wall came down, Germany became one country again. Historians write about this in history lessons, so you will meet the phrase «the fall of the Berlin Wall» often.
explain: Capital letters are your clue. «Berlin Zoo, opened in 1844, has one of the largest collections of animal species in the world.» Here Berlin is a name, so it tells you where the zoo is. Read the words around a name to see if it is a place, a person or a thing.
fact: Berlin is the capital city of Germany and its largest city.
fact: Berlin stands on the River Spree.
fact: «The Berlin Wall» divided East Berlin from West Berlin during the Cold War.
fact: When the Berlin Wall came down, Germany became one country again.
fact: «Berlin Zoo», opened in 1844, had a polar bear cub called Knut who became world-famous in 2007.
exercise: Berlin is the capital city of Germany. What kind of place is Berlin? | A mountain | *A city | A country | A river
exercise: In history lessons, what was the Berlin Wall? | *A wall that split Berlin into East and West | A bridge over the River Spree | A road to the airport | A wall around the zoo
exercise: Why is «Berlin» written with a big B? | Because it always starts a sentence | Because it is a feeling | Because it is a type of animal | *Because it is the name of a place
test: «Berlin Zoo, opened in 1844, has one of the largest collections of animal species in the world.» Which polar bear cub became world-famous in 2007? | Snowy | Ursa | Blizzard | *Knut
test: What happened to Germany when the Berlin Wall came down? | It split into two | *It became one country again | It moved to the sea | It stopped being a country
exam: Which best describes Berlin? | *A capital city, and the largest city in Germany | A small village with a famous bear | A type of animal found in zoos | A river that flows through a zoo
